{
  "id": "kv_cache_mechanism",
  "title": "KV Cache Bottlenecks",
  "category": "mechanism_deepdive",
  "domain_taxonomy": "neural_attention",
  "hook_tag": "MECHANISM DEEPDIVE",
  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": 1,
      "text": "Every time you run a long-context LLM, your GPU wastes up to 80% of its VRAM on fragmented, unused memory blocks. It is pure chaos.",
      "visual_focus": "A grid of memory blocks showing massive gaps of empty space between allocated tokens.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "wastes up to 80%": "#EF4444"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "GPU",
        "action_verb": "wastes",
        "direct_object": "VRAM",
        "anchor_word": "wastes",
        "semantic_role": "state_transition"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "grid_memory",
        "title": "VRAM FRAGMENTATION",
        "sub": "Standard KV Cache Allocation",
        "accent_color": "#EF4444",
        "params": {
          "fragmentation_ratio": 0.8
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 2,
      "text": "Think of it like a library bookshelf where every book is glued to a fixed position. If you need space, you are stuck with empty gaps.",
      "visual_focus": "Bookshelf animation showing fixed-size slots that cannot be rearranged, creating empty gaps.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "fixed position": "#F59E0B"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Library",
        "action_verb": "constrains",
        "direct_object": "storage",
        "anchor_word": "stuck",
        "semantic_role": "analogy_setup"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "grid_memory",
        "title": "THE BOOKSHELF PROBLEM",
        "sub": "Static Memory Allocation",
        "accent_color": "#F59E0B",
        "params": {
          "flexibility": "none"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 3,
      "text": "Enter PagedAttention. It borrows from OS virtual memory, slicing the KV cache into non-contiguous blocks that the GPU can map dynamically on the fly.",
      "visual_focus": "Blocks shifting into a compact, contiguous layout using a page table pointer system.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "PagedAttention": "#10B981"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "PagedAttention",
        "action_verb": "slices",
        "direct_object": "KV cache",
        "anchor_word": "dynamically",
        "semantic_role": "mechanism_intro"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "ast_tree",
        "title": "PAGED ATTENTION",
        "sub": "Dynamic Block Mapping",
        "accent_color": "#10B981",
        "params": {
          "paging_enabled": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 4,
      "text": "By decoupling the logical sequence from physical VRAM, we eliminate internal fragmentation entirely, allowing the model to pack requests tightly into the memory buffer.",
      "visual_focus": "Code snippet showing the page_table.find_free() call filling gaps instantly.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "decoupling": "#38BDF8"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Kernel",
        "action_verb": "allocates",
        "direct_object": "blocks",
        "anchor_word": "decoupling",
        "semantic_role": "technical_deep_dive"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "chalkboard_code",
        "title": "KERNEL LOGIC",
        "sub": "allocate_kv_block(token_id)",
        "accent_color": "#38BDF8",
        "params": {
          "code_snippet": "def allocate_kv_block(token_id): page = page_table.find_free()"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 5,
      "text": "The result? vLLM hits 1,180 requests per second\u2014a massive 78.8% throughput jump over standard caching. Efficiency is the new speed.",
      "visual_focus": "Bar chart comparing vLLM Paged (1180) vs Standard (660) vs No Cache (240).",
      "highlight_words": {
        "78.8% throughput jump": "#10B981"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "vLLM",
        "action_verb": "outperforms",
        "direct_object": "standard cache",
        "anchor_word": "jump",
        "semantic_role": "empirical_victory"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "horizontal_race_bars",
        "title": "BENCHMARK SHOWDOWN",
        "sub": "Requests Per Second",
        "accent_color": "#10B981",
        "params": {
          "hero": "vLLM Paged"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 6,
      "text": "Follow The Model Verse for daily deep-dives into how AI actually works under the hood. Stop wasting your compute.",
      "visual_focus": "Logo animation with a call to action overlay.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "The Model Verse": "#38BDF8"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Viewer",
        "action_verb": "follows",
        "direct_object": "The Model Verse",
        "anchor_word": "deep-dives",
        "semantic_role": "takeaway"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "chalkboard_code",
        "title": "THE MODEL VERSE",
        "sub": "Subscribe for more",
        "accent_color": "#38BDF8",
        "params": {
          "loop": true
        }
      }
    }
  ],
